WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:11.860
Italy is the only country, alongside with
Greece, that is poorer now than before having

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.230
the EURO as their official currency.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:19.800
The figures leave no space for doubt; Italians
now have less purchasing power than before,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.450
making them one of the few countries that
became worse off after joining the European Union.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:35.930
We are talking about the second biggest industrial
power in all of Europe, only surpassed by Germany.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.820
In fact, during the 90s, Italians were wealthier
than the British and the French.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:44.429
If you are my age or older, you might remember
EROS RAMAZZOTTI, LUCIANO PAVAROTTI or the

00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:46.539
so-called SPAGHETTI WESTERNS.

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:47.719
Yes, my dear viewers…

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:50.879
Italy was one of the biggest powerhouses on the planet.

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:53.429
And all despite their Government and their
ruling class.

00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:56.350
The political history of Italy is…

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:57.579
How should I say it?...

00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:02.079
Next to it, Game of Thrones would look like
Gilmore Girls.

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:08.930
Just remember: Italians have the Sicilian
COSA NOSTRA, the Calabrese N’DRANGRETTA,

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.960
the Napolitan CAMORRA

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.110
and many other gangs.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:17.980
And yes, all of them have important connections
with the highest level politicians.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:21.549
But there is more than Mafia here!

00:01:21.549 --> 00:01:25.530
During the Cold War, some government officials
helped extreme right wing terrorist groups

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.570
that organized the most violent attacks you
could imagine.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:31.149
And what about the extreme left wing?

00:01:31.149 --> 00:01:33.360
Well, they didn’t stay quiet either.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.210
The Red Brigades kidnapped and murdered an Italian Prime Minister.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:43.789
Look, if you’re into scary stories, you
should google something about Propaganda Due.

00:01:43.789 --> 00:01:47.689
Or you can just watch the movie ‘Il Divo’
from Paolo Sorrentino.

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:51.909
You will discover a fascinating country where
politics are everything but boring.

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:53.159
And now you might wonder….

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:55.189
What’s going on in Italy now?

00:01:55.189 --> 00:01:59.750
Do they have as much instability as they did
in the 70s and the 80s?

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.840
And the answer is, oh you bet they do!

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.840
IN just 10 years, Italy has had 6 different
prime ministers.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.109
In just 10 years!

00:02:06.109 --> 00:02:09.850
In other words, Keeping up with Italian politics
is an impossible mission.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:14.010
And this is why, in this video, we will not
talk about the Italian elections that have

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:19.250
been celebrated recently… not even about
Berlusconi’s love life.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.530
Because the real question here is…

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:26.040
How is it possible that such a chaotic country
could manage to become that wealthy?

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:31.230
And what is happening now, after two decades
of economic stagnation?

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:35.569
Today we are going to answer both of these
questions but before we do, let’s take a

00:02:35.569 --> 00:02:43.470
look back at The Good, the Bad and The Ugly
of Italian history.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.790
GIULIO ANDREOTTI IS…

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:47.159
“THE GOOD”

00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:52.430
During the 40s, the Italian Communist party
was the biggest of its kind all across Western

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:53.430
Europe.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:58.450
With more than 1,300,000 members, they could
win an election anytime.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:02.849
As you can imagine, in the middle of the Cold
War, this was something America could not

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:03.849
let happen.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:06.409
So…
do you remember the MARSHALL PLAN?

00:03:06.409 --> 00:03:10.599
If you’ve been following VisualPolitik for
a long time, you already know that Uncle Sam

00:03:10.599 --> 00:03:15.340
sent lots and lots of money to Europe so they
could rebuild their destroyed cities.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:22.450
When it came to Italy, this money was not
only meant to help the country but also to

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:27.230
finance the only political party who could
face the communist threat.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:30.830
This party was called the CHRISTIAN DEMOCRACY.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:35.540
“Mother, save your children bolchevism!

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.870
Vote Christian Democracy!”

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:41.079
During the following 50 years, Italy had 30
different prime ministers.

00:03:41.079 --> 00:03:42.079
Yep, you heard that right.

00:03:42.079 --> 00:03:45.870
This means the average age for an Italian
government was little more than a year and

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:46.870
half.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:53.290
But they all had something in common: most
of them were CHRISTIAN DEMOCRAT governments.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:59.930
And within the CHRISTIAN DEMOCRATS is a man
you should know.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:05.340
His name was GIULIO ANDREOTTI, the man who
became Prime Minister 7 different times, and

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.670
the real godfather of Christian Democracy.

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:15.530
For years, no Italian politician could do
anything without being blessed by Mr. Andreotti.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:21.430
“Power wears out those who don´t have it”
—Giulio Andreotti

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.620
And now you might wonder…

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.880
What did Christian Democrats stad for?

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.880
Well…

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.150
Christian Democracy was, basically, what we
call a catch-up-all-party.

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:33.220
Anyone except a communist could find his or
her place inside of this party.

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:38.570
And this included deals with the Napolitan
CAMORRA, the Sicilian COSA NOSTRA and, allegedly,

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:42.210
extreme right wing groups that terrorized
the country during the 80s.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:45.580
But we will talk about this in another video.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:50.880
The important thing is, Andreotti and his
Christian Democrats badly needed the popular

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:51.880
support.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:52.880
You know,

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:53.970
you need to win some elections.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:59.620
And, in order to do that, what’s better
than employing people with a good salary?

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:00.620
You see…

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:04.250
Italy has over 3.5 million civil servants
and they are among the highest paid in the

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:05.250
entire World.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.090
This means a crazy amount of public spendng
and lots of bureaucracy.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:14.620
In fact, since Andreotti’s time until now,
Italy is famous for two things: red tape and

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.440
ineffective courts.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:21.100
For a better understanding, let’s imagine
we have a company that produces construction

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.750
machines and we have a client who doesn’t
pay.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:29.430
We take him to the courts, right?

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:34.070
If we are in, say, France, this process will
take us around 2 and half months.

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:39.960
Well, in Italy we could wait more than 3 years
before we get our problem solved.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:43.890
As you can imagine, this is not the best business
climate.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:44.890
But nevertheless…

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:49.330
I said Italy became one of the wealthiest
countries in all of Europe, right?

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:50.880
How is that possible?

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:57.090
Well, my dear VisualPolitik viewers… the
answer lies in the ITALIAN LIRA.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:00.919
Yep, you heard that right… having their
own currency, the Italian Central Bank could

00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:05.440
devaluate anytime they needed to put their
economy on steroids.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.930
And now you might wonder…

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:09.930
But…

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:10.930
Simon!

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.001
Isn’t this the worst thing you could do?

00:06:13.001 --> 00:06:16.889
For instance, in this other video, I told
you that Germany became Rich, partly, because

00:06:16.889 --> 00:06:19.720
they had a very stable currency, the DEUSTCHE
MARK.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:22.800
And now I’m telling you the opposite.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:27.520
How is it possible that Italy Could grow so
much, having so much corruption, red tape

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.990
and devaluations?

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:34.790
Well, let’s take a look!

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.800
ROCCO SIFFREDI IS “THE UGLY”

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:43.229
Having acted in more than 1700 movies, Rocco
Siffredi, AKA, the Italian Stallion, dominated

00:06:43.229 --> 00:06:47.979
the adult section of rental stores worldwide
during the 80s.

00:06:47.979 --> 00:06:54.240
And yet, he is a symbol of Italian economy
during that time.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:58.000
A growth model that relied, heavily on…
inflation.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:02.870
You see, during the 80s and the 90s, Italy
flooded the world markets with…

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:03.870
CHEAP PRODUCTS.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:06.509
They were kind of a 20th century China.

00:07:06.509 --> 00:07:10.120
As soon as something worked in some other
country, some Italian company would show up

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:12.070
making the same thing, but… cheaper!

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:14.350
Here is an example: western movies.

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:18.830
In America, John Wayne movies were incredibly
successful.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:25.300
So Italian movie producers started doing more
of the same, but at an industrial level.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:28.530
This is how the Spaghetti western was born.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:32.690
And the same happened with other industries.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:36.789
While Donna Summer was making the entire world
dance, Italians struck back with SABRINA,

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:38.650
who did the same but…

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:40.509
CHEAPER and more explicitly!

00:07:40.509 --> 00:07:43.039
And what about Animated movies?

00:07:43.039 --> 00:07:46.979
While Disney was launching Aladdin in movie
theatres, the cheap, Italian version, was

00:07:46.979 --> 00:07:52.190
already available in all the video clubs.

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:57.300
But they cheaply reproduced more than culture
here!

00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:01.960
In general, Italian companies mastered the
art of making cheap things or, as the economists

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:05.159
would say, “low added value manufacturing”.

00:08:05.159 --> 00:08:08.710
Italy produced clothes, furniture and plastic
items.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:13.150
If you bought an animated action figure in
the 90s, it probably had a “Made in Italy”

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:14.150
label somewhere.

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:18.660
But if you bought a Stereo Sound system, it
would have a Made in Germany or Made in Japan

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:19.660
label.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:21.240
And now the questions is…

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:25.849
Why was the Italian economy so strongly based
on selling cheap things abroad?

00:08:25.849 --> 00:08:27.440
Well… look at this chart.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:31.169
Here you can see the value of the Italian
LIRA against the GERMAN MARK.

00:08:31.169 --> 00:08:35.580
As you can see, during the 80s and the 90s,
Italian currency was losing value all the

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:36.580
time.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:41.820
In 1980, you would get 450 Liras for 1 German
Mark.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:45.180
15 years later, you could get 1000 liras for
1 German Mark.

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:46.180
So what does this mean?

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:50.890
It means innovation was way more expensive
for Italian companies than German ones.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:55.280
For instance, imagine we have an Italian production
company during the 80s, and we want to make

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:57.510
a really innovative movie.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:02.160
Something like Star Wars, with state of the
art special effects and cutting edge technology.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:05.100
If we want to do that, we’re going to need
to buy that animation software that’s produced

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.960
in Japan, and those special cameras from America
that allow us to make battle scenes.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:11.770
But, since our Italian currency is losing
value all the time, those things are more

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:12.830
expensive for us.

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:14.550
Add to this the fact that, for anything we
do, any shooting outdoors we want to plan

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:18.140
or any new cameraman we have to hire, we need
to cut through never-ending red tape.

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:23.000
This doesn’t sound good, does it?

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:27.440
Now imagine that, instead of making a Star
Wars-like film, we call our friend Rocco Siffredi

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:28.630
and make a

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.630
adult movie with him.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.860
We just need a couple of cameras, a room and
a bed.

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:36.530
And… since we have a weak currency, we can
sell our movies abroad for a lower price than

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:37.530
any other film.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:47.770
So… with this model, the Italian economy
grew sky high…

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:50.550
During these years, thousands of small companies
were born.

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:51.930
But make no mistake!

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:54.660
Italian SMEs had nothing to do with German
SMEs.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:58.550
You see, German Mittlestands had between 50
and 200 workers.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:03.300
And they had enough scale to invest money
on research and innovation.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:07.600
Italian companies were way smaller, their
methods were more traditional, and their industries

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:10.580
were… well, more illegal…

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:16.040
…when Italy started taking account of its
shadow economy, (…) which makes up about

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:17.410
a fifth of Italian

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:18.410
GDP.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.750
As a result, the economy grew by 18% overnight

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:23.170
So now you might wonder…

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:27.920
Why should Italians innovate so much if they
were doing well by not doing it?

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.770
Well… now I will tell you why…

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:34.300
SILVIO BERLUSCONI IS “THE UGLY”

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:37.100
This is, finally, the 21st century.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:39.460
Christian Democracy is not that important
anymore.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:44.980
Now, the brand new leader of the center right
wing is this man you see on the screen…

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:47.780
his name is SILVIO BERLUSCONI.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:53.690
I have little hair because my brain is so
big it pushes everything else out.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.190
—Silvio Berlusconi

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:57.890
2002 was not the best year to be the Italian
Prime Minister.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.260
DO you know why?

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:05.270
Well, because 2002 was the year Italy abandoned
the Italian Lira and started using the EURO.

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:07.520
And what’s the main characteristic of the
EURO?

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.830
Here, no government can decide, by itself,
how to devaluate it.

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:16.230
Euros are issued by the European Central Bank,
which includes representatives of all the

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:17.370
member countries.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:21.610
This was a big problem for a country like
Italy, who had become so addicted to devaluation.

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:23.200
But things don’t stop there!

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.690
Do you remember another thing that happened
at the beginning of the 2000s?

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:27.690
Oh really?

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:28.690
You don’t remember?

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:32.040
Well, let me refresh your memory!!

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.860
China joins the World Trade Organization - at
last

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:36.360
And now you might wonder…

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:38.840
What does China have to do with the Italian
economy?

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.100
Oh man… a lot!

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:45.340
The fact that CHina had joined the World Trade
Organization was a symptom of something bigger.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:48.240
It meant that all of Asia was flooding the
international markets.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.770
It was not only China.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:55.130
Other countries like Thailand and Bangladesh
were already becoming big manufacturing powerhouses.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:56.290
And… surprise!

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:57.290
Surprise!

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:59.900
What did these countries start manufacturing
first?

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:00.980
Exactly!

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:01.980
Cheap things!

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:05.380
The same as the Italians did… but even cheaper!

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:11.580
Back then, Germany was already a behemoth,
technology wise.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:15.520
So, despite the Asian competition, their products
were still competitive.

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:18.440
Meanwhile, Italy could not go back to good
old devaluation.

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:20.870
First, they were part of the euro now.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:25.180
Second, devaluating wasn’t a solution against
Asia’s cheap salaries.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:28.680
Here is an example: one of the most symbolic
Italian companies is FIAT.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:32.360
In 1990, they sold over 1,300,300 cars in
Europe.

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:41.990
Now, they just sell 700,000 and they can’t
get into new markets.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:47.820
Other brands like BMW still maintain their
shares on their traditional markets and they

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:50.560
are growing in emerging countries like China.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:53.290
But wait a minute because things don’t stop
here!

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.840
Do you remember how Italy had over 3 million
civil servants?

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.600
Well, they are still there!

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.430
And they have to be paid!

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:04.160
In other words, while the Italian economy
is falling, their government collects less

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:07.130
and less taxes, but spending remains the same.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:08.660
SO what does this mean?

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:13.390
It means Italy is now the 4th most indebted
country on the planet.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.980
Their public debt is over 130% of their GDP.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:22.610
And this, my dear viewers, is just CRAZY!

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.210
Italy Is Europe's Next Big Problem

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:28.710
So now the question is…

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:34.180
Should Italy abandon the euro so they can
go back to their devaluation and cheap

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:35.460
manufacturing model?

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:40.170
Or maybe they should follow the German model
and let their companies innovate?

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:43.690
Please, leave your answer in the comment section
below.

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:45.310
And… sorry what did you just say?

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:48.020
You don’t know how the German economic model
works?

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:53.450
Oh come on, just click on this other video
and you’ll learn everything you need to

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.950
know about Germany’s economy!

